\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Returning an edge coefficient to its source}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{An edge coefficient is based at its source. Reflection
reverses that edge, so its new source is the original head.
The orientation sign alone therefore does not return the
coefficient to its declared fiber. How does the link transport
enter the pullback, and how does that pullback act on the
paired field generators?}
